#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:11
msgid "Adding Physics to Your Tileset!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:12
msgid "LET'S GET STARTED!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:14
msgid "In this tour, you learn how to add collision shapes to your tileset tiles."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:17
msgid "You'll create physics layers and add rectangular collision shapes to make tiles solid so the player can stand on a platform."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:20
msgid "In the next tour, you'll learn how to set up one way collision for platforms the player can jump through from below and stand on."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:36
msgid "Collisions in tilemaps"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:39
msgid "The tiles in a tilemap start without collision shapes. This means that when you draw tiles, by default, they are just visual elements without any physics properties."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:40
msgid "You need to add collision shapes to relevant tiles to make them solid and stop the player from falling through them."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:41
msgid "Before we can add collision shapes, we need to add a [b]Physics Layer[/b] in the TileSet to enable collisions on it. We can do that by editing the TileSet resource in the [b]Inspector[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:46
msgid "Selecting the Ground node"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:52
msgid "Make sure that the [b]Ground[/b] node is selected to reveal its properties in the [b]Inspector[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:58
msgid "Reveal the TileSet physics layers"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:64
msgid "Let's reveal the physics layers in the [b]Inspector[/b]:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:65
msgid "1. Click the [b]Tile Set[/b] property to expand the TileSet resource if it isn't already open"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:66
msgid "2. Locate and click the [b]Physics Layers[/b] category to open it"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:72
msgid "Creating a physics layer"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:76
msgid "The physics layers start out empty, so we need to create a new one."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:77
msgid "Click the [b]Add Element[/b] button under the [b]Physics Layers[/b] section to add a new physics layer."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:81
msgid "Add a physics layer to the [b]TileSet[/b] resource"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:92
msgid "Understanding collision layers"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:96
msgid "You now have one physics layer associated with your tileset!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:97
msgid "Just like Godot's physics bodies and area nodes, this physics layer comes with two important properties: [b]Collision Layer[/b] and [b]Collision Mask[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:98
msgid "These properties work the same as any other physics body or area node in Godot. Let's review each of them."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:103
msgid "The collision layer property"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:107
msgid "The [b]Collision Layer[/b] controls which physics layer the tilemap is on. It allows [b]other[/b] objects to detect the tilemap's platforms."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:108
msgid "Think of it as a \"tag\" the physics engine uses to identify the tilemap. It allows entities like the player character to stand on platforms."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:109
msgid "The player character is set up to look for ground on collision layer 2, so we need to change the [b]Collision Layer[/b] from [b]1[/b] to [b]2[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:110
msgid "Click the lit field labeled [b]1[/b] below \"Collision Layer\" to disable it, then click the field labeled [b]2[/b] to enable it."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:114
msgid "Set the collision layer to 2"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:128
msgid "The collision mask property"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:132
msgid "The [b]Collision Mask[/b] controls which other physics objects the tilemap itself can detect."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:133
msgid "We don't need the tilemap to detect anything - we just want the player character to be able to detect the tilemap."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:134
msgid "Let's remove the [b]Collision Mask[/b]. Click the lit field labeled [b]1[/b] below \"Collision Mask\" to disable it."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:138
msgid "Remove the collision mask 1"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:149
msgid "Opening the TileSet editor"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:155
msgid "Let's open the [b]TileSet editor[/b] to add collision shapes to our tiles."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:159
msgid "Open the TileSet editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:166
msgid "Activating the Select tool"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:172
msgid "We want to add the same collision shape to all our solid ground tiles at once. For that, we need to select them all."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:173
msgid "First, let's make sure we have the right tool active. Click the %s [b]Select Tool[/b] in the TileSet editor toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:177
msgid "Activate the Select Tool"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:185
msgid "Selecting all tiles"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:191
msgid "Now let's select all the solid ground tiles at once."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:192
msgid "Click and drag from the top left tile to the bottom right tile to select all the solid ground tiles in the tiles view."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:193
msgid "Use the zoom controls at the top left of the tiles view to zoom in and out if needed. Press the [b]Middle Mouse Button[/b] to pan the view."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:198
msgid "Accessing physics properties"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:202
msgid "Selecting one or more tiles reveals their properties in the middle column of the TileSet editor. This column works like the [b]Inspector[/b] dock: it shows the properties of the selected tiles."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:203
msgid "In the middle column, expand the [b]Physics[/b] section and then [b]Physics Layer 0[/b] to access the physics properties of the selected tiles."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:208
msgid "Expanding the TileSet editor"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:214
msgid "The TileSet editor can sometimes be too small to see all the properties. We can expand it to fill the entire Godot editor vertically by clicking the [b]Expand Bottom Panel[/b] button (Shift+F12) at the bottom right of the TileSet editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:215
msgid "This button works for all bottom panels in Godot, so you can use it to quickly resize the editor to your liking."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:219
msgid "Expand the bottom panel"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:227
msgid "The collision shape editor"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:233
msgid "Now, we can see the tiles' physics properties more comfortably. Let's focus on the [b]Physics Layer 0[/b] section once more."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:234
msgid "This section offers an editor to add collision shapes to the selected tiles. It works similarly to the [b]CollisionPolygon2D[/b] node, as it allows you to draw polygons to define the collision shapes."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:239
msgid "The collision shape editor toolbar"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:243
msgid "The toolbar above the collision shape editor contains several buttons to add, select, and remove points from the collision shape."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:244
msgid "On the right, the %s [b]Grid Snap[/b] icon lets you choose whether to snap the points to a grid or not. This is useful for aligning the points of the collision shape to pixel-perfect positions."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:249
msgid "Adding a square collision shape"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:253
msgid "Now let's add a collision shape. We want every tile to have a rectangular collision shape that covers the entire tile."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:254
msgid "For that, we can use the [b]Reset to default tile shape[/b] menu option:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:255
msgid "1. Click the %s [b]three vertical dots[/b] button in the collision shape editor toolbar"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:256
msgid "2. Select [b]Reset to default tile shape[/b] from the menu"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:257
msgid "You can also press the [b]F[/b] key with the collision shape editor focused."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:261
msgid "Add a square collision shape to the selected tiles"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:273
msgid "Verifying the collision shapes"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:279
msgid "You should now see a light blue polygon overlaid on each of your selected tiles in the tiles view on the right."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:280
msgid "Because all your tiles are selected, you just created a collision shape for all of them at once! This is a great way to save time when working with large tilesets."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:285
msgid "Running the scene"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:291
msgid "Let's test our collisions by running the scene."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:292
msgid "Click the [b]Run Current Scene[/b] button to run the game."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:293
msgid "Here are the controls to move the character:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:295
msgid "Use the arrow keys to move"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:296
msgid "Press the [b]C[/b] key to jump"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:298
msgid "Now, the character should be able to stand on the platforms instead of falling through them!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:306
msgid "Marvelous!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:307
msgid "CONTINUE"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:309
msgid "You now have a tileset with working collision shapes that can interact with physics bodies."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:312
msgid "Your progress will be saved if you quit now."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_adding_collision_shapes/103_adding_collision_shapes.gd:315
msgid "In the next tour, we'll learn how to set up one-way tiles that the character can jump through from below and stand on."
msgstr ""
